knowledge-is-a-lack-of-ignorance-5 = unlines (cons "**The divisions the primitive of hyperactivity removes.** The primitive is identity as paths, with univalence. A cut is any boundary drawn to make a field. Analysis carries across it along paths, and what a cut can and can't see is itself a theorem. The divisions that fall, each with the place in the design that already contains its removal, are logic | mathematics | computer science; discrete | continuous mathematics; the systems subfields; hardware | software; symbolic AI | statistical learning; linguistics | computer science | philosophy of meaning; biology | neuroscience | computation; human–computer interaction | theory; ethics | political philosophy | engineering; psychiatry | philosophy of mind | sociology; sociology | media studies | computing; pure | applied; and the humanities | the sciences." nil)
